The '''1993 Slovak presidential elections''' were held between 26 January and 15 February 1993. Michal Kováč was elected as the first [[president of Slovakia]] and became the only Slovak president elected by Parliament.<ref>{{cite news|author=<!-- no byline -->|title=Prehľad výsledkov prezidentských volieb od roku 1993|date=26 February 2014|url=http://www.teraz.sk/slovensko/prehlad-vysledky-prezidentske-volby/75255-clanok.html|website=[[Teraz.sk]]|accessdate=10 August 2016|language=sk|archive-date=27 August 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160827051857/http://www.teraz.sk/slovensko/prehlad-vysledky-prezidentske-volby/75255-clanok.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|first=Vladimír|last=Jancura|title=Prvý prezident mohol byť len Kováč|url=http://spravy.pravda.sk/domace/clanok/259024-prvy-prezident-mohol-byt-len-kovac/|website=[[Pravda (Slovakia)|Pravda]]|accessdate=10 August 2016|language=sk-SK|date=15 February 2013|archive-date=29 August 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160829063131/http://spravy.pravda.sk/domace/clanok/259024-prvy-prezident-mohol-byt-len-kovac/|url-status=live}}</ref> A candidate needed to receive 90 votes to be elected.

